---

Suggested Daily Schedule

If you're working a normal job:

Monday–Thursday: 2 hours each evening

Friday: Review and bug fixes (1–2 hours)

Saturday: 5–6 hours of focused development

Sunday: Rest or documentation (optional)


That gives you roughly 15–18 focused hours per week, which is enough to complete the MVP without constant late nights.

Final recommendation

Your CTO's stack choice—Next.js + Clerk + Prisma + MySQL—is well suited for this plan. Keep the MVP focused on the core business of listing, booking, renting, selling, and paying. Once that's stable and users are getting value, you can layer in Smart Trust™, blockchain, GIS, BIM, tokenization, and AI as version 2 features without destabilizing the core platform.
